      "explanation": "The `ids` query parameter is split by commas and directly concatenated into a raw SQL string passed to `session.execute(text(...))`. This allows an attacker to inject arbitrary SQL commands (e.g., `1; DROP TABLE orders; --`) because no parameterization or strict allowlisting is applied.",
      "evidence": [
