          "source": null,
          "content": "raw_ids = request.args.get(\"ids\", \"\")\n    id_list = raw_ids.split(\",\")\n    joined = \", \".join(id_list)\n    session = get_session()\n    rows = session.execute(\n        text(\"SELECT id, status FROM orders WHERE id IN (\" + joined + \")\")\n    )",
          "snapshot": null,
          "snapshot_conflict": false,
          "grounded_in_pr": true
        }
      ],
      "suggested_fix": "Use parameterized queries. For example, generate a list of placeholders (e.g., `:id_0, :id_1`) and pass the individual IDs as a dictionary of parameters to `session.execute(text(...), params)`. Alternatively, use the ORM's `in_()` method with a list of validated integer IDs.",
